figdown 0.1 block
# spec §12.3: absent is OMITTED, and an explicitly EMPTY label is a
# WRITTEN value — a third state, recorded uniformly on every
# label-bearing directive and on `title` (`EMPTY-LABEL-STATE`, 0.1;
# DISCREPANCIES `EMPTY-LABEL-DIRECTIVE-COVERAGE` resolved). The companion fixture
# 214-label-absent-vs-id freezes the absent half: read the two goldens
# together and the rule is the contrast between them. The id
# substitution is a RENDERING rule that applies only to absence, so
# every label written below draws nothing at all.
#
# The fixture wrote NINE empty labels until this release and now writes
# eight: `plane over ""` stood after `title ""` and the directive left the
# language (`PAINT-ORDER-CONSTRUCT`), taking its row with it. `bundle bl "" a--b` stood after
# the `edge` line and did NOT leave — `bundle` is declared by `topology`
# only since `SCENE-KEYWORD-MEMBERSHIP`, so it moved to section 2 rather than being dropped.
title ""
node a ""
group g ""
external x ""
node b "" in=g
edge a -> b
bitfield hdr "" numbering=lsb0
field "ver" 4
table t ""
| A |
|---|
| 1 |
timing w ""
signal clk 0101

figdown 0.1 topology
node a ""
node b ""
edge a -> b
bundle bl "" a--b
